se coupling from the wet EC probe. The buffer is also powered from the main 3.3 V rail, so the isolated SCL is level-shifted through a domain it should not share. Behaviour and isolation are compromised on this channel.\", \"confidence\": 0.5}], \"summary\": \"The EC channel's isolated SCL line contains an unspecified 74LVC1G34 buffer (U8) referenced to main GND and powered from +3V3, while the SDA line and the pH channel connect directly through the ADM3260; this bridges the isolated and main ground domains and departs from the specified direct isolated I2C path. Other power, feedback, and gate networks checked were consistent with their stated roles.\"}",
